        <div class="quiz-item" id="q2">
          <div class="quiz-q">
            <span class="qnum">Question 02 / 05</span>
            A PE file section shows an entropy value of 7.8 out of 8.0. What does this most likely indicate?
          </div>
          <div class="options">
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">A</span>The section contains normal executable code</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">B</span>The section is empty and unused</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">C</span>The section is packed, encrypted, or compressed — likely obfuscated payload</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">D</span>The section contains readable string data</button>
          </div>
          <div class="feedback-msg" id="fb2"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q3 -->
        <div class="quiz-item" id="q3">
          <div class="quiz-q">
            <span class="qnum">Question 03 / 05</span>
            During dynamic analysis, malware checks <code>IsDebuggerPresent()</code> and immediately exits. What type of evasion technique is this?
          </div>
          <div class="options">
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">A</span>Anti-VM detection</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">B</span>String obfuscation</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">C</span>Anti-debug detection</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">D</span>Domain generation algorithm (DGA)</button>
          </div>
          <div class="feedback-msg" id="fb3"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q4 -->
        <div class="quiz-item" id="q4">
          <div class="quiz-q">
            <span class="qnum">Question 04 / 05</span>
            A VirusTotal report shows 0/72 detections for a file submitted for the first time 2 hours ago. What is the correct interpretation?
          </div>
          <div class="options">
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">A</span>The file is definitely safe and can be executed freely</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">B</span>0/72 on a brand-new submission does not confirm safety — it may be a novel zero-day sample</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">C</span>The file is from a trusted source since no engine flagged it</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">D</span>VirusTotal is broken and should not be trusted</button>
          </div>
          <div class="feedback-msg" id="fb4"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Q5 -->
        <div class="quiz-item" id="q5">
          <div class="quiz-q">
            <span class="qnum">Question 05 / 05</span>
            Which Windows API imports in a PE's import table are the strongest indicators of process injection capability?
          </div>
          <div class="options">
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">A</span>MessageBox and ExitProcess</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">B</span>CreateRemoteThread, VirtualAllocEx, and WriteProcessMemory</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">C</span>GetTickCount and Sleep</button>
            <button class="opt-btn"><span class="opt-letter">D</span>RegOpenKey and RegCloseKey</button>
